PART 1: AWS CLOUD FUNDAMENTALS
What is AWS?
Amazon Web Services is a cloud computing platform that provides on-demand infrastructure services such as:
	• Compute 
	• Storage 
	• Networking 
	• Databases 
	• Security 
	• Monitoring 
	• Machine Learning 
	• DevOps tools 
Instead of purchasing physical servers, organizations rent resources from AWS and pay based on usage.

