Interview Question:
Q: What is an AWS Region?
Answer:
An AWS Region is a physical geographic area that contains multiple isolated Availability Zones. Customers select regions based on latency, compliance, and availability requirements.

Availability Zone (AZ)
An Availability Zone is one or more physically separate data centres inside a region.
Example:

Mumbai Region
|
    |
-----------------
|       |       |
AZ-A   AZ-B   AZ-C
Benefits:
	• High availability 
	• Fault tolerance 
	• Disaster recovery 
