Interview Question
Q: Explain AWS Shared Responsibility Model.
Answer:
AWS is responsible for security of the cloud, including physical infrastructure and hardware.
Customers are responsible for security in the cloud, including applications, data, IAM permissions, and operating system configuration.

AWS Pricing Models
1. On-Demand
Pay only for what you use.
Suitable for:
	• Short-term workloads 
	• Testing environments 
Example:
Development server running for a few days.

2. Reserved Instances
Commit to AWS usage for 1 or 3 years.
Benefits:
	• Lower cost 
	• Predictable workloads 
Used for:
	• Production databases 
	• Long-running servers 

3. Spot Instances
Uses unused AWS capacity.
Advantages:
	• Very cheap 
Disadvantages:
	• AWS can terminate instances when capacity is needed 
Used for:
	• Batch jobs 
	• Testing 
	• Data processing 

